{
  "case_id": "c44_fallback_precise_flag_reads_the_look_back",
  "title": "The precise flag of an end on the 30-minute fallback reads its 7-day look-back and nothing more",
  "rules": ["pos_04", "lnk_01", "lnk_02", "lnk_04", "lnk_05"],
  "reasoning": [
    "Casey's Q1 answer, (c) (PR #66 comment 6968763406, item 2), as PR #67 words it in PLAN's data model: the positions a counted receipt read, \"which for a receipt on the 30-minute fallback are the positions in its 30-minute window and in its 7-day look-back, and nothing more\". precise_source is true when the box's cell was sent among those in at least one delivery that qualifies under pos_04 (D7).",
    "Each of c44-ra, c44-rb, c44-rc and c44-rd sent cell D (20 bits, about 1 km north of C) on the public broker at 22 09:05, cell C (20 bits, box c20) on the public broker on 23 October 5 minutes before its first receipt, and one more copy of cell C on MeshSTL only (seen_meshstl true, seen_public false). That copy has 20 bits, so it qualifies under pos_04.",
    "C and D neither overlap nor lie within 40 m of each other, so at every receipt each relayer has moved and takes the fallback; the only position within 30 minutes of any receipt is its public C. Every receipt uses c20; with the relayer not stationary, each receipt keeps its own relayer box, and c44-g, stationary on its 16-bit position of 22 09:00, is on its hour box, g16. The hour has one box per end (lnk_02, steps 5, 6 and 8).",
    "c44-ra's MeshSTL copy was sent at 21 10:10, two days before its receipts at 10:10, 10:20 and 10:30: inside every receipt's 7-day look-back and outside every 30-minute window. lnk_02 read it to find that c44-ra had moved, so relayer_precise_source is true. Reading only the 30-minute window (option (a)) or only the position taken (option (b)) would give false.",
    "c44-rb's copy was sent at 16 10:09, 7 days and 1 minute before its first receipt at 10:10: outside every receipt's look-back and every 30-minute window. No receipt read it, so relayer_precise_source is false.",
    "c44-rc's copy was sent at 16 10:10, exactly 7 days before its first receipt at 10:10. lnk_02: \"30 minutes and 7 days are both inclusive\" (Casey, issue #55, Q5; PR #66, Q2), so that receipt read it and relayer_precise_source is true. The receipts at 10:20 and 10:30 did not read it; the flag reads the union of the positions each counted receipt read (PLAN data model).",
    "c44-rd's receipts are at 10:05, 10:10 and 10:15 and its public C at 10:00. Its MeshSTL copy, at 10:46, is in the same clock hour but 31 minutes after the last receipt: no 30-minute window reaches it and no look-back reads forward. relayer_precise_source is false; the flag does not read the rest of the hour.",
    "gateway_precise_source is false in every hour: c44-g's only cell has 16 bits and was sent on the public broker.",
    "Every receipt is a direct hop (relay_node equals the relayer's own byte, lnk_01) and passes lnk_05 at 2745.603 m from c20 to g16. Each hour has 3 packets: kept. Medians: SNR 5, 6 and 7 dB give 6.0; RSSI -90, -95 and -100 dBm give -95.0. position_uncertainty_m is c20 22.734410 m plus g16 363.750397 m, = 386.484807 m (lnk_05)."
  ],
